# Unified station: runtime output
#
# ⚠️ COMMENTS MUST BE ON THEIR OWN LINE. Every pattern in this block used
# to carry a trailing `# explanation`, and git does NOT treat that as a
# comment: `#` only starts one at the START of a line. So the pattern was
# literally `logs/                  # rotating station.log`, which matches
# no real path, and NONE of these five directories was actually ignored.
#
# The visible symptom was a pull on the Pi aborting with "Your local
# changes to acoustic_radar/logs/station.log would be overwritten by
# merge" every time the station had run — the log was being tracked, and
# every run made it dirty.

# rotating station.log
logs/
# WAV clips saved around each alarm
detections/
# regenerated by `python hud.py`
_hud_preview/
# regenerated by `python radar_overlay.py`
_radar_preview/
# per-installation overrides (like radar_calibration.json).
#
# ⚠️ STILL TRACKED ON PURPOSE, despite this line. Untracking it now would
# make the next pull DELETE it on the Pi, taking camera_role_id_hint with
# it and putting the cameras back to fail-closed OFFLINE. It is listed
# here so it stops being *added* fresh elsewhere; see the note in
# PROJECT_REPAIR_VALIDATION.md about moving installation config out of git
# once the station is calibrated.
fusion_config.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
